From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: add a Samsung S5K3L6 sensor driver

The Galaxy Z Flip3's (SM-F711N) rear ultrawide module carries a Sony
IMX258 or a Samsung S5K3L6. Samsung's firmware ships a CamX sensor module
for each (com.samsung.sensormodule.2_sony_imx258.bin and 2_lsi_s5k3l6.bin)
and its camera HAL has the kernel match each one's chip ID to find the
fitted one. Mainline has no S5K3L6 driver.

This one has stock's settings for the sensor: chip ID 0x30c6 at 0x0000,
I2C address 0x2d, the module's init settings and its 4000x3000 30 fps
mode (4 lanes), stream on (mode_select, then 0x3c1e = 0) and off, and its
power-up order (VANA, VDIG, VIO, MCLK at 19.2 MHz, reset released 18 ms
before the first access). Exposure at 0x0202, analogue gain at 0x0204
with 0x0020 as 1x up to stock's 16x, frame length at 0x0340, flips and
test patterns as on the S5K3M5, whose driver this one follows.

The output PLL in the mode settings is 19.2 MHz / 3 x 89 = 569.6 MHz,
which is also the 1139 Mbps per lane stock writes to 0x0820, so that is
the link frequency; the pixel rate is stock's output pixel clock, 478 MHz
(4896 x 3253 x 30 fps). The unflipped Bayer order is GBRG (stock's colour
filter arrangement 2). Only built from the stock data: no S5K3L6 unit has
been tried.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
